<given-names>YA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Improvement of coverage and utilization of EmOC services in southwestern Bangladesh</article-title><source>Int J Gynaecol Obstet</source><year>2005</year><volume>91</volume><fpage>298</fpage><lpage>305; discussion 283-4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16226760</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ijgo.2005.06.029</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Islam</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Haque</surname><given-names>YA</given-names></name><name><surname>Waxman</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhuiyan</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Implementation of emergency obstetric care training in Bangladesh: lessons learned</article-title><source>Reprod Health Matters</source><year>2006</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>72</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16713880</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0968-8080(06)27229-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><source>Bangladesh Demographic and Health Survey, 1999-2000</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>Dhaka, Bangladesh and Calverton, Maryland, USA , National Institute of Population Research and Training, Mitra and Associates, ORC Macro</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mitra</surname><given-names>SN</given-names></name><name><surname>Al-Sabir</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Cross</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Jamil</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><source>Bangladesh Demographic and Health Survey, 1996-1997</source><year>1997</year><publisher-name>Dhaka, Bangladesh and Calverton, Maryland, USA , National Institute of Population Research and Training, Mitra and Associates, Macro International Inc.</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mitra</surname><given-names>SN</given-names></name><name><surname>Nawab</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Islam</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Cross</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Saha</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><source>Bangladesh Demographic and Health Survey, 1993-1994</source><year>1994</year><publisher-name>Calverton, Maryland, USA , National Institute of Population Research and Training, Mitra and Associates, Macro International Inc.</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Filmer</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Pritchett</surname><given-names>LH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Estimating wealth effects without expenditure data--or tears: an application to educational enrollments in states of India</article-title><source>Demography</source><year>2001</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>132</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11227840</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bell</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Curtis</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Alayon</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><source>Trends in Delivery Care in Six Countries. DHS Analytical Studies No. 7</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Calverton, Marlyand, USA , ORC Macro, International Research Partnership for Skilled Attendance for Everyone</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><sur